WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.130
Every family answers the same
hourly calendar only question.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.027
Training uses eight thousand,

00:00:07.027 --> 00:00:10.350
six hundred and forty five
hours in twenty eleven,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.310
followed by the same four thousand, three
hundred and fifty seven validation hours.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.050
No weather, target transform or
demand history is introduced.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.590
The final test remains reserved.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.330
Different fitting algorithms
do different work,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.780
so pretending a tree split and an SGD
update are equal operations would not

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.270
create a fair control.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.310
We instead expose each familys
structural limits, search allowance,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.790
stopping rule and actual costs.

00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:47.843
Each tree family receives three
configurations and the same three declared

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:50.673
seed values, giving nine main fits.

00:00:51.423 --> 00:00:54.213
Across families that is twenty seven fits,

00:00:54.443 --> 00:00:58.373
plus four deterministic references
with no newly tuned settings.

00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:04.623
A small training only timing pilot checks
feasibility for each family before the

00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:05.313
full sweep.

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:08.173
These pilots choose no quality setting.

00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:13.793
Every fitted main state is saved and
hashed before validation is opened.

00:01:14.563 --> 00:01:17.773
The configured timing guards
run after a fit returns;

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:20.873
structural caps bound the actual model.

00:01:21.503 --> 00:01:25.073
We do not describe those checks
as interruptible hard timeouts.

00:01:27.358 --> 00:01:30.368
For one configuration and output policy,

00:01:30.518 --> 00:01:35.088
take every declared seeds validation
MAE and average those scores.

00:01:35.578 --> 00:01:37.788
This is an average of
quality measurements,

00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:40.348
not an ensemble of the three seed models.

00:01:41.038 --> 00:01:45.508
Exact ties prefer raw output and then
the declared configuration order.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:49.928
The first seed supplies a representative
artifact by prior declaration.

00:01:50.518 --> 00:01:53.168
We never pick the seed with
the most flattering score.

00:01:53.718 --> 00:01:57.378
The result record keeps both
the configuration mean and that

00:01:57.378 --> 00:01:58.588
representatives score

00:01:58.978 --> 00:02:02.928
so the selected artifact and reported
evidence can be understood together.

00:02:05.315 --> 00:02:11.165
The grouped mean remains best at ninety
one point five seven mean absolute error.

00:02:11.935 --> 00:02:16.695
The best tree is near one hundred and the
best forest near ninety nine point seven

00:02:16.695 --> 00:02:17.285
five.

00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:22.175
Clipped interaction linear regression
is near one hundred point five two,

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:26.425
and clipped boosting near one
hundred and two point two two.

00:02:27.295 --> 00:02:32.035
Beating raw additive linear regression
is not enough when a stronger simple

00:02:32.035 --> 00:02:33.605
reference already exists.

00:02:34.455 --> 00:02:37.325
We therefore retain
groups with raw policy.

00:02:37.955 --> 00:02:41.385
Its outputs are already nonnegative,
so clipping ties.

00:02:42.035 --> 00:02:44.965
Keeping that model is the result
of the completed comparison,

00:02:45.435 --> 00:02:48.065
not evidence that the
implementation was abandoned.

00:02:50.358 --> 00:02:55.078
The representative deep forest fits
locally in about zero point six eight

00:02:55.078 --> 00:02:59.468
seconds and saves about sixteen
point one megabytes of JSON.

00:03:00.478 --> 00:03:04.798
Replaying the validation batch takes
roughly one tenth of a second through our

00:03:04.798 --> 00:03:07.008
inspectable numerical traversal.

00:03:07.678 --> 00:03:12.638
The three hundred stage booster fits in
about zero point eight two seconds and

00:03:12.638 --> 00:03:15.428
saves about six hundred
and sixty four kilobytes.

00:03:15.998 --> 00:03:19.848
These observations describe this
machine and this implementation.

00:03:20.618 --> 00:03:23.718
JSON bytes measure storage
rather than peak memory,

00:03:23.718 --> 00:03:27.748
and replay is not optimized
library serving latency.

00:03:28.438 --> 00:03:33.248
We compare costs honestly without
manufacturing a universal speed ranking.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.330
Eighty three checks and an independent
audit verify the saved predictions,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:41.530
scalar metrics,

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.410
leaf membership, identities

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.690
and fitted state replay.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.350
All written explanations were completed
before creating these companions.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.500
These checks establish
implemented behavior,

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.570
while the learners own explanation
remains a separate conversation.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.790
The same validation period has
informed multiple development choices,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.770
so its selected score can be optimistic.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.110
The final test and
application remain pending.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.600
The useful next question is why a more
detailed historical partition predicted

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.730
the busy Monday worse
than a broader group.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.810
That interpretation is the purpose
of this practical comparison.

